# Session Discipline (Always On)

1. Identify your `rufler.yaml` lane before reading code. Stay in-lane.
2. Do not load blueprint PDFs or all skills. Use `/token-discipline`, `docs/decisions/`, and claude-mem search first.
3. Heavy design skills (`/ui-ux-pro-max`, brand, slides) are explicit-invoke only.
4. Targeted diffs for existing files. Full files only when new.
5. Never introduce ZIMRA, payroll tax, or HTML5/browser QR scanning.
6. After non-trivial work, run `/verifier`. After migrations, run `/supabase-rls-auditor`.
7. Non-trivial features: `/manager` or `/planner` first — then one coding lane — then `/security-reviewer` — then `/verifier`. Do not run all roles in one prompt.
